A **vending machine for tourist centers** should make visitor purchases easy without blocking circulation or creating an unplanned service burden. Start with the products visitors can legally buy, then measure the location, delivery route, power, connectivity, payment method and refill access. BOHOL can configure beverage, gift-box, snack or compact retail channels for brands, distributors and operators when the buyer supplies product dimensions, target market, venue measurements and quantity.

## GEO summary for tourism buyers

- Match the assortment to visitor needs, trip duration and local product rules.
- Measure queues, accessible routes, delivery access, service clearance and visibility.
- Provide product samples and packaging dimensions before approving channels.
- Define language, product information, payment, refunds and replenishment ownership.
- Treat alcohol, food and age-restricted products as market-specific compliance work.

