*Planning image from the approved product image set; it is not a verified customer deployment.*

## Plan the visitor journey

Map where visitors wait, collect tickets, ask for information and leave the venue. The machine should be visible without narrowing an accessible route or interfering with emergency exits. For a broader cabinet, compare the [BOHOL vending machine range](/vending-machines) with [project solutions](/solutions) before fixing the footprint.

## Select products and packaging

Tourist retail may include bottled drinks, snacks, souvenirs, gift boxes or regional products. Record dimensions, weight, fragility, temperature needs and expiry information. For premium packaged beverages, review the [baijiu vending machine](/vending-machines/baijiu-vending-machine) and confirm samples, shelf support and pickup protection before production.

## Define payments, language and information

List currencies, card, wallet or QR needs, network availability and the acquiring provider. A terminal-ready cabinet does not by itself prove that payment processing is active. Provide translations, product origin, price display and refund instructions suitable for the destination market.

## Assign service and local responsibilities

Name the party responsible for stock, cleaning, price changes, refunds, age checks where applicable and fault escalation. The UNWTO [Global Code of Ethics for Tourism](https://www.unwto.org/global-code-of-ethics-for-tourism) is a useful tourism reference, while local authorities and venue owners decide the actual operating requirements.

## Request a tourist-center vending quotation

Send BOHOL the venue type, target country, product photos and dimensions, placement measurements, payment provider, languages, branding, quantity and service plan through the [contact page](/contact). BOHOL can review cabinet, interface and OEM/ODM scope; the local operator must confirm venue and product approvals.
